= Northern Illinois University

During my time as a graduate student at NIU, I worked variously as a recitation leader or as a grader for
a variety of our undergraduate courses. I also worked each semester as a tutor in NIU's Math Assistance
Center. I typically would spend about 3 to 8 hours per week tutoring students on a walk-in basis. Here,
I would tutor students in any of our undergraduate math courses between MATH 101 and real analysis.

