= Selected Student Feedback

/"This course was fairly challenging starting off. I was definitely putting in up to 10 hours outside of class, however I did not graduate high
school and got my GED at seventeen\eighteen. I haven't done much schooling since so maybe that's why I felt like it was moving really
fast at first but after our first exam it seemed like Mr. Herbig pulled back a bit and I found that extremely helpful. I was really grateful he
was paying attention to us and tailored his lectures to suit our understanding a bit more. Overall, I had a fantastic experience."/ 
 - Kishwaukee College, College Algebra (Spring 2025)

 /"He is a great TA and tried his best to get the class to ask any questions that we had for problems. He made it very aware that this is
a place to ask questions so we were never confused on the test and if one solution wasn't working for someone hed try and explain
it in a different way."/
 - Northern Illinois University, Discrete Mathematics (Fall 2025)

/"Mr. Herbig always presented the topics we covered in class in a slightly different way which would just help us even more when
trying to understand the topic. He has a really good understanding of the materials we have covered in class and was always
available to answer questions."/
 - Northern Illinois University, Discrete Mathematics (Spring 2026)

